WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.490 --> 00:00:01.790
- [Instructor] We've already learned

00:00:01.790 --> 00:00:03.600
that when we multiply by 10,

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:05.560
let's say we took the number 53

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:08.290
and we were to multiply it by 10,

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:11.040
it has the effect of
shifting all the digits

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:12.800
once place to the left.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:14.760
So, this should be a review for you.

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:17.493
But this was going to be 530.

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:22.680
And we could see that what
used to be in the tens place

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:26.370
has been shifted to the
left, to the hundreds place.

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:27.960
And what used to be in the ones place

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:31.520
has been shifted to the
left to the tens place now.

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:33.580
And we saw, if you divide by 10,

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:35.220
you have the opposite effect.

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:38.930
And so, let's say if I had 120,

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:41.140
I could say, let's divide by 10,

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:46.140
I could also say this is the
same thing as 120 times 1/10.

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:48.120
What is going to happen there?

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:49.700
Well, in this situation,

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:53.870
all the digits are going to
shift one place to the right.

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:55.700
So, what used to be in the tens place

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:57.900
will now be in the ones place;

00:00:57.900 --> 00:00:59.400
what used to be in the hundreds place

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:01.030
will now be in the tens place.

00:01:01.030 --> 00:01:03.560
So, this is just going to be equal to 12.

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:04.850
So, that was all review.

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:06.530
But now were going to
extend this a little bit

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:10.140
by thinking about things
that have place values

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:12.530
representing less than a
one, I guess you could say,

00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:14.660
or we're gonna deal with decimals.

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:17.700
So, just to get ourselves warmed up,

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:20.363
let's see if we could
figure out what 3.015

00:01:22.870 --> 00:01:25.690
times 10 is.

00:01:25.690 --> 00:01:28.433
Pause this video, and see
if you can figure that out.

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:32.390
Well, the exact same
thing is going to happen.

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:35.910
All of our digits are going to
shift one place to the left.

00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:39.450
So, right now, we have a
three in the ones place,

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:42.930
we have a zero in the tenths place,

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:45.860
we have a one in the hundredths place,

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:49.470
and we have a five in the thousandths,

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:51.060
thousandths place.

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:54.230
But now, they're all going to
shift one place to the left.

00:01:54.230 --> 00:01:57.190
So, the three is now going
to into the tens place,

00:01:57.190 --> 00:01:59.630
it's going to shift one place to the left.

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:02.940
So, we're going to
have, in the tens place,

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:05.510
we are now going to have our three.

00:02:05.510 --> 00:02:09.420
And now, this zero, which
was in the tenths place,

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:13.540
is now going to shift into the ones place.

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:17.030
So, the zero is going to go right over,

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:18.980
the zero's going to go right over there.

00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:22.630
That is now in the ones place.

00:02:22.630 --> 00:02:25.090
And them we'll put our decimal.

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:30.090
And now, what's going to
go into the tenths place

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:33.050
and the hundredths place?

00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:37.010
And actually, I'll rewrite
the thousandths place as well.

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:39.660
This one is going to shift
one place to the left,

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:42.170
into the tenths place,

00:02:42.170 --> 00:02:44.050
so into the tenths place.

00:02:44.050 --> 00:02:46.900
And then the five that was
in the thousandths place

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:49.180
is now going to shift
one place to the left,

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:51.630
into the hundredths place,

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:54.120
so into the hundredths
place, just like that.

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:56.710
Now, we could put a
trailing zero over here,

00:02:56.710 --> 00:02:59.140
but that's not going to change
the value of this number,

00:02:59.140 --> 00:03:00.530
so I'll just leave it like that.

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:01.860
And so, there you have it.

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:05.000
We see that every digit has
shifted one place to the left.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:08.493
So, this is equal to 30.15.

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:11.340
I'll just put that zero there for kicks.

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:13.820
And so, we could think
about the other way around.

00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:18.330
What if I were to take 67.5,

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:21.500
and if I were to divide it by 10,

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:23.500
or another way of thinking about it is

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:26.260
if I were to multiply this by 1/10.

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:27.680
Pause the video, and see if you can

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:29.430
figure out what that's going to be.

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:33.200
Well, now, every digit is going to shift

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:34.980
one place to the right.

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:37.280
So, the six is going to
be in the ones place,

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:41.280
the seven is going to go
into the tenths place,

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:45.230
and then the five is going to
go into the hundredths place.

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:46.110
So, let's write that out.

00:03:46.110 --> 00:03:49.240
So, I have six is going
to go into the ones place,

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:50.730
and then we're gonna
have our decimal point,

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:53.450
our seven is going to go
into the tenths place,

00:03:53.450 --> 00:03:57.750
and then our five is going to
go into the hundredths place.

00:03:57.750 --> 00:03:59.973
So, there you have it, we get 6.75.

